how to stop all docker service

Apr 19
Run this inside your MarketPulse folder where your docker-compose.yml is:

bash
docker-compose down
This stops and removes all containers. Your PostgreSQL data is safe — it's saved in the postgres_data volume.

Other useful commands:

bash
# Stop containers but don't remove them (faster restart)
docker-compose stop

# Start them again after stop
docker-compose start

# Restart all containers
docker-compose restart

# Stop AND delete everything including volumes (wipes PostgreSQL data)
docker-compose down -v
For daily use, docker-compose stop and docker-compose start are the quickest — containers resume in seconds without re-downloading anything.

